Well, you have three doors, no idea of what lie behind them, one key that
can only open one door (or maybe luck penalty for opening more than one
door in that level or for breaking door) and cryptic sentence writen on
doors (or engraved on the floor in front of them), like
"One of the three sentence is false"
"My left neighboor lead to the stairs"
...
You have to think to find which of the sentence are true and which are
false (this king of enigma is very classical, I guees you can find tons of
them in Smullyan's book among other) and choose which door you want to
open. One of the door leads to the stairs, other to nothing (or small
useful objects in high level, or small useless object (loadstone)
elsewhere, or big monsters (bigger than normally found on those levels),
or even some kind of instadeath if you want to be mean).

This should not be hard to implement (only need to change the luck code to
give penalities for opening/breaking more than one door [or introduce
special keys/doors]) and may give a break from Sokoban.

