Slash'em seems to have three "aligned" keys that are the only way to open
certain doors in Vlad's tower. So you have to do the three aligned
"quests" in order to grab those keys and say hello to Vlad. Those kind of
keys could be use in a logical-enigma game. But as I've explained before,
you don't even need that, luck penalty for opening too many doors should
be enough (plus somekind of almost instadeath behind the wrong door such
as an hostile Archon who is surely to big to do something else than run at
this point of the game).

I think those enigma may even be generated a little more randomly than
Sokoban levels and thus prevent to many learning/spoilers. Things may even
be mixed (normal Soko level plus one door to choose at the entrance or
exit).

